---
description: Guardrails for the Relentless app. Use the PRD as source of truth. Do not invent missing product details.
alwaysApply: true
---

Use `docs/PRD_relentless.md` as the source of truth for this project.

Hard rules:
- Do not invent product features, UX flows, pricing details, onboarding details, formulas, or engagement logic that are not explicitly defined in the PRD.
- Keep architecture/server-authority/security/monetization decisions aligned with the PRD.
- Prefer minimal diffs. Do not refactor unrelated files.
- Preserve known-good behavior unless the task explicitly changes it.
- If a required low-level detail is missing, do not guess. Output `Human Input Needed` and list the missing decisions.
- For implementation tasks, change only the files needed for that task.
- For planning tasks, separate output into:
  1. Confirmed from PRD
  2. Open questions
  3. Proposed narrow file changes
- Do not silently choose subscription details, trial length, pricing, paywall copy, exact formulas, or exact UX details.
- Treat the app as subscription-based, iOS-first, Apple IAP/StoreKit + Superwall, as defined in the PRD.
- Assume the same base stack as the current app unless the task explicitly says otherwise.
- For lesson content: do not paraphrase **exercise** copy (interactive model, step text, option labels, coach-authored exercise strings). Transcribe approved scripts verbatim into JSON/migrations per `content/CONTENT_DELIVERY_GUIDE.md` (Section 4a “Verbatim exercise copy”, Section 5) and `content/DEVELOPER_IMPL_GUIDE.md` (Section 1 checklist, Section 3 “Verbatim exercise copy”).
- Exercise content steps are tap-to-advance. Do not implement time-locks, lock countdowns, or auto-advance for typed entry, multi-select, or text-card steps — even if an approved script asks for them. Breathing rhythm timers (e.g. `box_breathing`, body-scan zone timers) remain timed.
- After adding or editing files under `supabase/migrations/`, run `npx supabase db push` from the repo root (or `supabase db push` if the CLI is on PATH) before finishing the task, unless the user explicitly says not to push migrations. Do not end the task by only telling the user to run migrations when you can run them yourself. If the CLI is unavailable, the project is not linked, push fails, or non-interactive confirmation is not possible, say so and give the exact commands to run locally.
- After changing code under `supabase/functions/`, run `supabase functions deploy <function-name>` from the repo root for each modified function (and any function that bundles changed `_shared` imports) before finishing the task, unless the user explicitly says not to deploy. If the CLI is unavailable or login fails, say so and give the exact deploy commands.
- Before any EAS iOS production build or `--auto-submit`, increment `expo.ios.buildNumber` and `expo.android.versionCode` in `mobile/app.json` (and bump `expo.version` if App Store Connect rejects a duplicate marketing version). Commit those version bumps before running `eas build`. Do not rely on EAS remote auto-increment; `appVersionSource` is `local`.
